[Event "London"]
[Site "London ENG"]
[Date "1912.10.29"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Edward Lasker"]
[Black "George Alan Thomas"]
[Result "1-0"]
[ECO "A84"]
[Opening "Dutch Defence"]
[CMIntro "A famous king hunt: after a queen sacrifice the black king is chased all the way across the board to g1."]

1. d4 e6 2. Nf3 f5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. Bxf6 Bxf6 6. e4 fxe4 7. Nxe4 b6
8. Ne5 O-O 9. Bd3 Bb7 10. Qh5 Qe7 11. Qxh7+ {The queen sacrifice begins the
hunt.} 11... Kxh7 12. Nxf6+ Kh6 13. Neg4+ Kg5 14. h4+ Kf4 15. g3+ Kf3 16. Be2+
Kg2 17. Rh2+ Kg1 18. Kd2# {The black king has travelled from g8 to g1 - and is
mated by a quiet king move.} 1-0

